DE07 -- the wide-binary ANGULAR statistic on Gaia EDR3: re-run of the registered directional-EFE test
====================================================================================================================
  registered prior:  A-hat = +2.95 at p = 0.029 with the AQUAL-class sign
                     (old corpus first firing of the directional-EFE test on ROTATION CURVES; a different
                      statistic than the wide-binary split -- see the prior status report below)
  AQUAL-class amplitude: L = 0.27 -> ~6% velocity modulation -> A_PRED = 0.060 in split units (r ~= dv/v)
  PRE-REGISTERED KILL CONDITIONS (written before any measurement):
    K1  widest-bin s/r_M > 1.96 split PARALLEL-dominant at >= 3 sigma on the RANDOM-AXIS null
        -> direction-blind rule ABSENT (modulation PRESENT)
    K2  widest-bin split |r|/e_axis <= 2 sigma on the random-axis null -> direction-blind SURVIVES (ABSENT)
    K3  anything else, or the two a0 footings disagree -> UNDECIDED
  MUTATE = 0 (1 breaks the RUWE-clean-cut hinge)
  El-Badry+2021 Gaia EDR3 catalogue: 1817594 pairs loaded
  clean sample (R_chance_align < 0.01, RUWE < 1.4 both, d < 250 pc, parallax S/N > 50 both, 4 < M_G < 11 both, |dmu|/sigma > 5): 39702 pairs
  pairs with a well-defined sky orientation: 39702; <cos^2 phi>_GC = 0.4894 (isotropic 0.5)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MEASUREMENTS
  SAMPLE-LEVEL (2-30 kAU): N = 8146 (4078 perp, 4068 par); b_perp/b_par - 1 = +0.0068 +- 0.0106 (random-axis 1000 axes, seed 2001), p = 0.522; bootstrap would say +- 0.0134
  WIDEST BIN s/r_M > 1.96 (canonical footing, r_M(1 Msun) = 7959 AU): N = 372 (177 perp, 195 par); b_perp/b_par - 1 = -0.1530 +- 0.0926 (random-axis, seed 3196), p = 0.093; bootstrap would say +- 0.0408  PAR-dominant
  WIDEST BIN s/r_M > 1.96 (alt       footing, r_M(1 Msun) = 7251 AU): N = 453 (217 perp, 236 par); b_perp/b_par - 1 = -0.1081 +- 0.0734 (random-axis, seed 3196), p = 0.176; bootstrap would say +- 0.0396  PAR-dominant
  
  POWER at the AQUAL-class amplitude: 3 sigma needs N = 8.0e+03 (21x this widest bin, canonical) and 6.1e+03 (13x, alt) at the measured random-axis errors
  context: a UNIFORM 6% split over the whole 2-30 kAU sample is excluded at 5.0 sigma -- the modulation can only live in the EFE-transition band, hence the widest-bin framing

