  prior status: the registered A-hat = +2.95, p = 0.029 is the old corpus firing of the directional-EFE test on rotation curves -- a different quantity from b_perp/b_par - 1; like-for-like comparison is not derivable at DR3 N. The DR3 wide-binary sample-level split (+0.0068 +- 0.0106, 0.6 sigma, p = 0.522) does not reproduce it and is consistent with zero; the AQUAL-class-sign hint is not confirmed by the wide-binary channel at DR3 N, which is underpowered for the ~6% modulation in the transition band (N_need ~ 7975 widest-bin pairs).  The hint's status rests on the rotation-curve channel where it originally fired, not on this re-run.
